[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m It is also the *lowest-level* entry point — there is no convenience wrapper and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no other non-static function in the library, so "exercise the low-level entry
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m points, not just the wrappers" collapses to: drive `update_frame_header`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m directly over its full input space.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "Options" are not function arguments here; they are the **struct fields the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m branches on**. Enumerated from the four `switch` statements and the nested
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `if`/`else if` chain in `c_src/src/lib.c`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Axis BS — `cur_blocksize`** (first `switch`, bits 12–15). 13 explicit
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `case`s + a 2-way `default` (`<= 256` vs `> 256`) ⇒ **15 classes**:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `192, 576, 1152, 2304, 4608, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192, 16384, 32768,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   default≤256, default>256`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Axis SR — `samplerate`** (second `switch`, bits 8–11). 11 explicit `case`s
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   + 6 `default` sub-classes ⇒ **17 classes**:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `882000, 176400, 192000, 8000, 16000, 22050, 24000, 32000, 44100, 48000,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   96000`, then `%1000==0 && /1000<256`, `%1000==0 && /1000>=256` (silent),
